:282,"side":"R","color":1,"_w":1572},{"id":"9nwweu5","text":"Imalat","children":[{"id":"tql4y4w","text":"değerlendirme","children":[{"id":"tq53p0f","text":"vize","children":[{"id":"yazk18h","text":"hoca bir konu verecek onun üzerinde sunum + rapor","children":[],"_h":46,"_w":300},{"id":"bg9hs14","text":"kounuyu hoca ile konuşarak değiştirebileceksin.","children":[],"_h":46,"_w":300}],"_h":99,"_w":618},{"id":"eiae1jv","text":"final","children":[{"id":"ux8hgye","text":"Rapor","children":[],"_h":28,"_w":61}],"_h":28,"_w":61},{"id":"9n2mls4","text":"gelişme","children":[{"id":"bibo520","text":"Subtopic","children":[],"_h":110,"img":{"id":"x6w1tr4gfwa70pz","ar":0.4256480218281037,"w":"M"}}],"_h":110,"collapsed":false}],"_h":251,"_w":697},{"id":"gnrdcsj","text":"yapılacaklar","children":[{"id":"h2vb73g","text":"derse çalışman yeterli şu an birşey yok","children":[],"_h":28,"_w":267}],"_h":28,"_w":267}],"_h":291,"side":"R","color":2,"_w":982},{"id":"ltiictd","text":"Seminer","children":[{"id":"rah4txz","text":"yapılacaklar","children":[{"id":"wc2vpv4","text":"13 üne kadar sunum konusunu belirleyip tabloya girmen lazım.","children":[{"id":"5kfrq64","text":"girdim","children":[],"_h":28},{"id":"8eqm5yg","text":"Presentation Topic\n\nAn Agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation System for Automated Quotation Preparation of Customized Industrial Press Machines","children":[],"_h":122},{"id":"j7xgtd3","text":"Abstract\n\nManufacturers of industrial press machines and production lines work in an engineer-to-order (ETO) environment. Each customer request needs a customized quotation that includes machine selection, engineering calculations, technical specifications, and a price. Today, engineers prepare these quotations manually. They repeat calculations, rewrite specifications from earlier offers, and depend on individual experience. This makes the process slow, inconsistent, and open to errors.\n\nThis thesis proposes an agentic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) system that supports engineers in preparing quotations, starting with mechanical and eccentric presses. The system builds a knowledge base from historical quotations, catalogs, and calculation sheets, using vector and structured databases. When a new customer requirement arrives, a Large Language Model (LLM) agent retrieves similar past cases and plans the task. It then calls deterministic engineering tools for press selection calculations, such as process force, energy per stroke, and the tonnage curve versus stroke position. Finally, it generates a draft quotation in which every technical value is traceable to a calculation or a source document. An engineer reviews, corrects, and approves the draft.\n\nA preliminary literature review shows that LLM and RAG methods have been applied to quotations for services and custom parts, and that classical expert systems have addressed press selection. However, no study was found that combines retrieval of historical ETO quotations with validated press engineering models for capital machinery. Recent work also reports that LLMs alone have low numerical accuracy in quotation tasks. The system will be evaluated on real industrial quotations and compared with LLM-only and RAG-only baselines. The metrics will be numerical accuracy, specification completeness, and preparation time. Future work will extend the approach to complete production lines and automatic layout generation.\n\nKeywords: Retrieval-Augmented Generation, LLM agents, engineer-to-order, quotation automation, mechanical presses, knowledge-based engineering","children":[],"_h":1104}],"_h":46,"_w":300,"collapsed":true},{"id":"qfm8ivv","text":"sunuma hazırlık","children":[{"id":"l68x5bg","text":"konu araştırma","children":[],"_h":28,"_w":119},{"id":"y9lg2rl","text":"vinh kursu uygulama","children":[],"_h":28,"_w":155}],"_h":63,"_w":292,"collapsed":false}],"_h":116,"_w":610},{"id":"89l7d8n","text":"sunum tarih","children":[{"id":"juf3nb3","text":"december 1","children":[],"_h":28}],"